# Line-ending policy.
#
# THE HASH-CHAINED LOGS MUST NEVER BE REWRITTEN BY GIT.
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this machine converts LF -> CRLF on checkout. For an
# append-only log whose tamper-evidence is `prev = sha256(previous raw line)`,
# that conversion changes the bytes every hash was computed over, so EVERY line
# after the first fails verification — the log reads CORRUPT while being
# perfectly intact. Measured 2026-08-02 on coordination/estate/kel.jsonl:
# 298 of 299 lines "chain-break", 0 breaks once the stray \r was stripped.
#
# It is invisible to `git status` (git normalizes back on the way in), and it
# fails toward "the hub holds nothing", which would have made a satellite sync
# re-stage the entire corpus as new. Pin these to LF everywhere.
*.jsonl        -text
*.ndjson       -text
governance.log -text

# Everything else: let git decide, but normalize text in the repo to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
